      "content": [],
      "prompt": [
        {
          "type": "markdown",
          "text": "Antonia purchased a box of pasta and some tomatoes at the grocery store. Antonia paid \\$2 for the\nbox of pasta and \\$1.10 per pound for the tomatoes. If Antonia paid a total of \\$7.50for the box of\npasta and the tomatoes, which of the following equations can be used to find $p$, the number of\npounds of tomatoes Antonia purchased? (Assume there is no sales tax.)"
        }
      ],
      "source": {
        "kind": "editable-pdf-source",
        "sourceSetId": "pdf-218b2d54e56c47bf892b8b7571b936f1",
        "sourceQuestionId": "m1-q1"
      },
      "options": [
        {
          "id": "choice-a",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "markdown",
              "text": "$$1.10 p+2=7.50$$"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "choice-b",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "markdown",
              "text": "$$1.10 p - 2=7.50$$"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "choice-c",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "markdown",
              "text": "$$1.10+2 p=7.50$$"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "choice-d",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "markdown",
              "text": "$$1.10 - 2 p=7.50$$"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
